Initial coming-soon site for Astroid Club.

The community home for $ASTROID holders, third surface in the Astroid
family alongside astroid.space (mission) and lounge.astroid.space
(freeroll poker).

What's in v1
- Single static landing page: header, hero, four "what's coming" tease
  cards, a non-interactive "waitlist opens soon" panel, family strip
  linking the rest of the Astroid surfaces, and a compliance footer.
- Theme variables and starfield CSS lifted from astroid.space so the
  family reads as one visual system.
- Security headers via proxy.ts (HSTS, CSP, COOP, CORP, X-Frame, etc.)
  matching astroid.space.
- All user-facing strings centralized in app/lib/branding.ts so a
  compliance review is a single-file diff.

What's intentionally NOT in v1
- No waitlist form, no email capture, no API, no Supabase.
- No wallet connect, no Solana SDK.
- No countdown timer to a date we don't have.
- No St. Jude or charity copy on this domain - that messaging stays on
  astroid.space/charity. Footer link only.

Compliance posture
- No price talk, no "100x" or "moon" copy, no implied future token value.
- No promises to holders. Drops described as discretionary, not earned.
- Token holding framed as community participation, not an investment.

Stack
- Next.js 16 + React 19 + Tailwind 4 + TypeScript strict.
- No three.js / r3f - the CSS gradient starfield is enough for a static
  page and saves us hundreds of KB of JS.

Verified clean: npm run typecheck and npm run build both pass.
